{"kind":"assert","text":"Join parity inventory at published main 8a9f9d1e49874479636b6186094767a6184db23f. I inspected the current entry points and compared their mode, custody and completion checks. This read-only inventory changes no files and runs no tests.\n\nPerson links. Start, CLI and local MCP share the explicit-pin parser in packages/client/src/invitation.ts:21–37. JP1 already shipped that parser with encoding/refusal tests and native CLI restart cases (notes/implementation/2026-11-11-person-invitation-parity.md:3–26). Start prepares and retains the signed envelope under its page key, then checks or submits that envelope and verifies the receipt (apps/room/page/src/data.ts:314–377 and join-custody.ts:76–139). The CLI keeps the exact envelope in its private store and validates the receipt and accepted entry before committing the configuration (packages/cli/src/command-membership.ts:88–184). Local MCP uses its configured signer and caller's idempotency key, retains the envelope, and reads the exact accepted Membership entry and its inbox send before saving the configuration (packages/mcp/src/service.ts:1078–1079,1642–1693). It uses the directory, rules and destination references from the link at that point.\n\nTagged links. Start's redemption parses person and device links (apps/room/page/src/data.ts:329–377). Its agent invitation UI issues the link (apps/room/page/src/main.ts:776–821). CLI dispatches agent, checker and device tags to their enrollment owners (packages/cli/src/command-membership.ts:88–92). Agent enrollment uses the shared client agent-key encoding, binds the full Membership/controller/member/invitation references and revisions, keeps the exact enrollment under filesystem custody, and checks directory and inbox (packages/client/src/agent-key-invitation.ts:21–42 and packages/cli/src/invitations.ts:388–456,549–556). Local MCP's join schema and handler accept person links only. Hosted MCP omits the generic join tool (packages/mcp/src/hosted-tools.ts:6–7). Its separate hosted enrollment (packages/mcp/src/hosted.ts:724–726) uses its own custody and does not close the local gap.\n\nCheck. Start checks the privately held original (apps/room/page/src/join-custody.ts:76–79). CLI join --check accepts tagged agent, checker and device links (packages/cli/src/line.ts:138). Local MCP join takes only link and idempotencyKey. Its retry resends retained bytes, so the schema has no check-only equivalent (packages/mcp/src/service.ts:1078–1079,1661–1666).\n\nNative Membership already judges the signed join and enrol acts, including the invitation selector (packages/platform/src/membership.ts:652–686). The remaining parity work is the tagged invitation and check paths, shared client-side validation where it still diverges, and the controller/directory/inbox completion proof. The local MCP native person and tagged key witness and valid/refused check comparison remain open. Source work stays in the request's later phase.","body":{"head":"8a9f9d1e49874479636b6186094767a6184db23f","inventory":"read-only"}}